      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-11666",
      ":question/problem": "One card is picked at random from a standard $52$-card deck.\nDefine $A$ to be the event \"the selected card is an ace.\" Which of the following statements are true regarding this event?\n\n1. $P(A) = 0.08$ to $2$ decimal places\n2. $A^{\u2032}$ is the event \"we get a king\"\n3. $P(A^{\u2032}) = 0.98$ to $2$ decimal places"
    },
