      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119661",
      ":question/problem": "Two fair $6$-sided dice are rolled. Define $A$ to be the event \"the sum of outcomes is a prime number\" Which of the following statements are true regarding this event?\n\nI. - $P(A)=0.42$ to $2$ decimal places\nII. - ${A}^{'}$ is the event \"the sum of the outcomes is an even number\"\nIII. - $P({A}^{'})=0.58$ to $2$ decimal places"
