      ":question/problem": "Two fair $6$-sided dice are rolled. Define $A$ to be the event \"the sum of outcomes is equal to $5.$\" Which of the following statements are true regarding this event?\n\nI. - $P(A)=0.15$ to $2$ decimal places\nII. - ${A}^{'}$ is the event \"the sum of the outcomes is less than $5$\"\nIII. - $P({A}^{'})=0.89$ to $2$ decimal places"
